{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For there is no bread and there is no water.</b> One may wonder — but was not the manna descending for them each and every day, and was there not an abundance of water for them from the miracle of the rock that was now newly wrought for them? But this was their complaint: they said, 'Behold, our situation is abnormal; we have no bread and water like the other nations. For the other nations, whether they are meritorious or liable, have bread to satiety, and all the more so water; but as for us, the essence of all our conduct and our food and our drink is in a novel manner, for we do not have bread for many days in a single day, like the other nations, whose souls are satisfied with the provision of food they see before them and with them. And it is not with us except day by day; and even the water, which is free to all the world and without which a person has no sustenance — it too was taken from us when Miriam died and the well ceased. And since all our affairs follow after punishment and reward, behold, we are conducted in a more novel manner than the other nations.' And furthermore, that bread which comes to us day by day is inferior bread (לחם קלוקל), and it is destined to spoil in the intestines, and our soul is nauseated by it — 'and is there any child of woman who takes in and does not let out?' And this is the evil report (דבה) they spread concerning the manna, which was for them an honor and a distinction, yet they found fault with it. For the merit of the wilderness generation, who were like the ministering angels, the manna came to them day by day so that their eyes would always be suspended toward HaShem, as it is written (Psalms 123): ״הנה כעיני עבדים אל יד אדוניהם״ and so forth; and the matter was to habituate their souls in the trait of trust (bitachon) and faith in the Name, blessed be He. And because they sinned by spreading evil report, they were punished with the punishment of the serpent, which spreads evil report — this is what is written: ״וישלח HaShem בעם את הנחשים השרפים״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: let the serpent, which eats many kinds and they are all one taste in its mouth, come and exact retribution from the eaters of the manna, who eat one kind and taste many kinds. And further, they were punished with this punishment, for these serpents with which they were punished were the very serpents that were in the wilderness, of many species — this is what is written (Deuteronomy 8): ״המוליכך במדבר הגדול והנורא״ and so forth; and for all forty years not one of Israel was harmed by them, for one of the seven clouds went before them and killed the serpents and scorpions so they would not harm them, and that cloud was specially designated for this marvel. And now in the fortieth year, when they spread evil report concerning a thing that was for them a good and excellent trait, the Holy One, blessed be He, sent against them the burning serpents. And this is why it does not say 'וישלח HaShem בעם נחשים שרפים' but rather 'את הנחשים השרפים' — the serpents that were in the wilderness, in the manner of (Exodus 8): ״הנני משליח בך את הערוב״, that is, the swarm that was in the wilderness; for there was no new creation for the moment, but the serpents and the swarm were already in the wilderness. And it was sufficient to say 'נחשים' and it added 'השרפים'; it is read 'השרופים' (the burned) but written 'השרפים' (the burning). And because until now the cloud had been burning them so they would not harm Israel, they were then 'השרופים' (the burned); but once Israel sinned, they became 'השורפים' (the burners). And the sense of <b>inferior bread (לחם הקלוקל)</b> is a term of contempt — the lightest of the light."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:38.489868158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}